  "body": "# Objective\r\n\r\nMake Dev containers first class citizens for zed users.\r\n\r\nDev containers offered no in-app way to manage the underlying container or to\r\nrecover once its connection dropped: users had to fall back to the CLI, and an\r\nunreachable container left the project stuck. On top of that, rebuilding or\r\nrestarting a container accumulated duplicate, stale entries because a container's\r\nidentity was tied to its ephemeral instance rather than the project.\r\n\r\nThis PR makes dev containers first-class, manageable resources and gives every\r\ndisconnect a clear recovery path.\r\n\r\nFixes #56576.\r\n\r\n> [!NOTE]\r\n> This PR was implemented with AI assistance, supervised by me. \r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n\r\n- **Lifecycle management** from the command palette, the title-bar remote\r\n  control, and the thread sidebar:\r\n  - **Reconnect** — reconnect, starting the container first if it stopped.\r\n  - **Restart** — stop and start the container (clearing wedged in-container\r\n    state), then reconnect.\r\n  - **Rebuild** — rebuild from scratch, then reconnect; also works from a local\r\n    project to (re)build its container.\r\n  - **Stop** — stop the container and reopen the project locally.\r\n  - **Delete** — stop and remove the container to reclaim resources, then reopen\r\n    the project locally.\r\n  - Destructive actions confirm first, and the current connection is always torn\r\n    down cleanly before the container is changed.\r\n- **Recovery when a connection is lost**, offering a Reconnect → Restart →\r\n  Rebuild ladder instead of a dead end: from the disconnected overlay (which\r\n  restarts a stopped container automatically), from failed operations' error\r\n  prompts, and from the agent thread view (which disables the message input and\r\n  shows a recovery callout so a message can't hang against a dead connection).\r\n- **Stable identity across rebuilds**: a dev container keeps a single identity\r\n  across open/stop/rebuild cycles, tied to the project rather than the container\r\n  instance, so entries in the sidebar and recent projects are no longer\r\n  duplicated and the persisted connection is reused and refreshed.\r\n- **Sidebar improvements**: multiple dev containers in one project (e.g. several\r\n  `devcontainer.json` files) are distinguishable by a subtitle and tooltip, and\r\n  **Delete Dev Container** is available directly from a project group's menu —\r\n  including for a stopped container with no open workspace.\r\n\r\nNote: deleting a container frees its resources but keeps the project's history\r\n(the sidebar entry remains, shown as disconnected, and can be removed\r\nseparately), and every lifecycle side effect runs only on an explicit user\r\naction.\r\n\r\n## Testing\r\n\r\n- Automated: `remote` (24), `dev_container` (117), `recent_projects` (33), and\r\n  `sidebar` (142) suites pass, including new tests for identity stability across\r\n  rebuilds, connection persistence reuse, and the sidebar Delete entry.\r\n  `title_bar`, `project_panel`, `workspace`, and `agent_ui` were compile-checked.\r\n- Manual (macOS, Docker): opened a dev container and exercised\r\n  reconnect / restart / rebuild / stop / delete from each surface; simulated a\r\n  dropped connection (stopping the container out-of-band) to verify the recovery\r\n  ladder in the overlay, error prompts, and agent thread; and confirmed an\r\n  open/stop/rebuild cycle reuses a single sidebar/recent-projects entry.\r\n- Reviewers can reproduce by opening a project in a dev container, using the\r\n  lifecycle actions from the title bar / sidebar / command palette, and stopping\r\n  the container via the CLI to trigger the recovery flows.\r\n- Not covered: Windows and Linux hosts were not tested.\r\n\r\n## Self-Review Checklist:\r\n\r\n- [x] I've reviewed my own diff for quality, security, and reliability\r\n- [x] Unsafe blocks (if any) have justifying comments\r\n- [x] The content adheres to Zed's UI standards ([UX/UI](https://github.com/zed-industries/zed/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md#uiux-checklist) and [icon](https://github.com/zed-industries/zed/blob/main/crates/icons/README.md) guidelines). With the notable exception that I could not test this on Linux or Windows.\r\n- [x] Tests cover the new/changed behavior\r\n- [x] Performance impact has been considered and is acceptable\r\n\r\n## Showcase\r\n\r\n> This section is optional. If this PR does not include a visual change or does not add a new user-facing feature, you can delete this section.\r\n\r\nNew user-facing surfaces:\r\n\r\n- Title-bar remote control opens a dev container menu (Reconnect, Restart,\r\n  Rebuild, Stop, Delete) when the active project is a dev container.\r\n- Disconnected callout in the agent thread and recovery choices in error prompts.\r\n- Sidebar project-group menu with a **Delete Dev Container** entry and\r\n  disambiguating subtitles.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/615d31de-c8dd-45b3-b612-325f5d46e9e8\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nRelease Notes:\r\n\r\n- Added dev container lifecycle management (reconnect, restart, rebuild, stop,\r\n  and delete) with automatic recovery when a dev container connection is lost.\r\n",
